    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Recognize speech from a local audio or video file and return ASR sentences.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input audio or video file path.\r\n          --language TEXT [auto]  \r\n                              Recognition language: auto, or a lowercase language tag such as\r\n                              zh-cn, en-us, or ja-jp. Input is case-insensitive.\r\n          --output TEXT       Optional: write the full ASR result JSON to this path.\r\n          --clear-talking-head \r\n                              Remove filler or redundant talking-head words and rebuild\r\n                              sentence timing.\r\n          --timeout <duration> [5min] \r\n                              Maximum ASR workflow duration. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s,\r\n                              or min. Bare numbers and m are invalid. Default: 5min. Range\r\n                              after conversion: 1ms..2147483647ms.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media asr --input /tmp/speech.m4a\r\n  $ lyra-cli media asr --input /tmp/clip.mp4 --language zh-cn --output /tmp/asr.json\r\n  $ lyra-cli media asr --input /tmp/interview.mp4 --clear-talking-head\r\n  $ lyra-cli media asr --input /tmp/interview.wav --timeout 5min\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - This command is auth-gated and checks subtitle-recognition membership entitlement.\r\n  - It only recognizes source speech; use media translate as a separate step.\r\n  - Talking-head cleanup is disabled by default and only runs when explicitly requested.\r\n  - It does not read or modify a draft.\r\n  - Video inputs are decoded to a temporary audio track in the runner.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Recognize speech from a local audio or video file and return ASR sentences.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input audio or video file path.\r\n          --language TEXT [auto]  \r\n                              Recognition language: auto, or a lowercase language tag such as\r\n                              zh-cn, en-us, or ja-jp. Input is case-insensitive.\r\n          --output TEXT       Optional: write the full ASR result JSON to this path.\r\n          --clear-talking-head \r\n                              Remove filler or redundant talking-head words and rebuild\r\n                              sentence timing.\r\n          --timeout <duration> [5min] \r\n                              Maximum ASR workflow duration. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s,\r\n                              or min. Bare numbers and m are invalid. Default: 5min. Range\r\n                              after conversion: 1ms..2147483647ms.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media asr --input /tmp/speech.m4a\r\n  $ lyra-cli media asr --input /tmp/clip.mp4 --language zh-cn --output /tmp/asr.json\r\n  $ lyra-cli media asr --input /tmp/interview.mp4 --clear-talking-head\r\n  $ lyra-cli media asr --input /tmp/interview.wav --timeout 5min\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - This command is auth-gated and checks subtitle-recognition membership entitlement.\r\n  - It only recognizes source speech; use media translate as a separate step.\r\n  - Talking-head cleanup is disabled by default and only runs when explicitly requested.\r\n  - It does not read or modify a draft.\r\n  - Video inputs are decoded to a temporary audio track in the runner.\r\n",
